    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's extend digit puzzles to three-digit numbers.\n\nWe will keep the hundreds, tens and units digits separate, build the number from place value, and then track what changes when digits swap or follow a relation.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For a three-digit number, let\nh = hundreds digit\nt = tens digit\nu = units digit.\n\nThen the number is\n100h + 10t + u.\n\nRemember: h cannot be 0, but t or u can be 0.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
